([SOLVED PROBLEM 1: Series RLC Circuit Impedance and Power Factor]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: A series circuit consists of a resistance R = 15 Omega, inductance L = 0.05 H,) Tj
T*
(and capacitance C = 100 microF connected across a 230 V, 50 Hz AC supply. Calculate: \(1\)) Tj
T*
(Inductive reactance X_L, \(2\) Capacitive reactance X_C, \(3\) Total impedance Z, \(4\) RMS) Tj
T*
(current I, \(5\) Power Factor cos\(phi\), \(6\) Active Power P.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Reactances at f = 50 Hz \(omega = 2 * pi * 50 = 314.16 rad/s\):) Tj
T*
(X_L = omega * L = 314.16 * 0.05 = 15.71 Omega.) Tj
T*
(X_C = 1 / \(omega * C\) = 1 / \(314.16 * 100 * 10^-6\) = 1 / 0.031416 = 31.83 Omega.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Total Net Reactance and Impedance:) Tj
T*
(Net Reactance X = X_L - X_C = 15.71 - 31.83 = -16.12 Omega \(Capacitive\).) Tj
T*
(|Z| = sqrt\( R^2 + X^2 \) = sqrt\( 15^2 + \(-16.12\)^2 \) = sqrt\( 225 + 259.85 \) = sqrt\() Tj
T*
(484.85 \) = 22.02 Omega.) Tj
T*
(Phase Angle: phi = arctan\(-16.12 / 15\) = arctan\(-1.0747\) = -47.06 degrees.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Compute Circuit Current:) Tj
T*
(I_rms = V_rms / |Z| = 230 / 22.02 = 10.45 Amperes.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Power Factor:) Tj
T*
(PF = cos\(phi\) = cos\(-47.06 deg\) = R / |Z| = 15 / 22.02 = 0.681 LEADING \(since X_C >) Tj
T*
(X_L\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 5: Active Power Consumed:) Tj
T*
(P = V_rms * I_rms * cos\(phi\) = 230 * 10.45 * 0.681 = 1,637 Watts = 1.637 kW.) Tj
T*
