T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: An RLC series circuit has R = 2 Omega, L = 1 mH \(10^-3 H\), and C = 0.1 microF) Tj
T*
(\(10^-7 F\) excited by a 10V AC generator. Determine: \(1\) Resonant frequency f_0, \(2\)) Tj
T*
(Quality factor Q, \(3\) Half-power bandwidth BW, \(4\) Voltage across inductor at resonance.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Calculate Resonant Frequency f_0:) Tj
T*
(f_0 = 1 / [ 2 * pi * sqrt\(L * C\) ] = 1 / [ 2 * pi * sqrt\( 10^-3 * 10^-7 \) ]) Tj
T*
(sqrt\(10^-10\) = 10^-5.) Tj
T*
(f_0 = 1 / [ 2 * pi * 10^-5 ] = 100,000 / \(2 * pi\) = 15,915.5 Hz ~ 15.92 kHz.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate Quality Factor Q:) Tj
T*
(Q = \(1 / R\) * sqrt\(L / C\) = \(1 / 2\) * sqrt\( 10^-3 / 10^-7 \) = \(1 / 2\) * sqrt\(10,000\) =) Tj
T*
(\(1 / 2\) * 100 = 50.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Calculate Bandwidth BW:) Tj
T*
(BW = f_0 / Q = 15,915.5 Hz / 50 = 318.3 Hz.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Current and Voltage Magnification at Resonance:) Tj
T*
(Current at resonance: I_0 = V / R = 10 V / 2 Omega = 5.0 Amperes.) Tj
T*
(Inductive reactance at resonance: X_L0 = 2 * pi * f_0 * L = 2 * pi * 15,915.5 * 10^-3 =) Tj
T*
(100 Omega.) Tj
T*
(Voltage across inductor: V_L = I_0 * X_L0 = 5.0 A * 100 Omega = 500 Volts.) Tj
T*
(Voltage Magnification Factor: V_L / V_supply = 500 V / 10 V = 50 = Q. \(Q-factor) Tj
T*
(magnifies terminal voltage 50-fold\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([SOLVED PROBLEM 3: Complete Power Triangle and Power Factor Correction]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: An industrial biotechnology plant motor load draws 50 kW at 400 V, 50 Hz with a) Tj
T*
(lagging power factor of 0.707. Determine: \(1\) Apparent power S1 and reactive power Q1,) Tj
T*
(\(2\) Capacitance required in parallel to improve the overall power factor to 0.95) Tj
T*
(lagging.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Initial Electrical Operating State:) Tj
T*
(cos\(phi1\) = 0.707 => phi1 = 45.0 degrees => tan\(phi1\) = tan\(45\) = 1.0.) Tj
T*
(Active Power P = 50 kW.) Tj
T*
(Initial Reactive Power Q1 = P * tan\(phi1\) = 50 * 1.0 = 50 kVAR.) Tj
T*
(Initial Apparent Power S1 = P / cos\(phi1\) = 50 / 0.707 = 70.72 kVA.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Desired Operating State with Improved Power Factor:) Tj
T*
(cos\(phi2\) = 0.95 => phi2 = 18.19 degrees => tan\(phi2\) = tan\(18.19\) = 0.3287.) Tj
T*
(New Reactive Power Q2 = P * tan\(phi2\) = 50 * 0.3287 = 16.44 kVAR.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Required Reactive Power Provided by Shunt Capacitor:) Tj
T*
(Q_C = Q1 - Q2 = 50.0 - 16.44 = 33.56 kVAR = 33,560 VAR.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Compute Required Capacitance C:) Tj
T*
(Q_C = V^2 * omega * C => C = Q_C / \(V^2 * 2 * pi * f\)) Tj
T*
