(Problem: Derive from first principles the RMS value, average value, and form factor of a) Tj
T*
(symmetrical half-wave rectified sinusoidal voltage waveform v\(t\) = V_m * sin\(omega * t\)) Tj
T*
(for 0 <= omega*t <= pi, and v\(t\) = 0 for pi <= omega*t <= 2*pi.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Calculate Average Value V_avg over full period T = 2*pi:) Tj
T*
(V_avg = \(1 / 2*pi\) * int_0^pi V_m * sin\(theta\) d\(theta\) = \(V_m / 2*pi\) * [ -cos\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(]_0^pi) Tj
T*
(= \(V_m / 2*pi\) * [ -\(-1\) - \(-1\) ] = \(V_m / 2*pi\) * 2 = V_m / pi ~ 0.318 * V_m.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate RMS Value V_rms:) Tj
T*
(\(V_rms\)^2 = \(1 / 2*pi\) * int_0^pi V_m^2 * sin^2\(theta\) d\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(Using sin^2\(theta\) = \(1 - cos\(2*theta\)\) / 2:) Tj
T*
(\(V_rms\)^2 = \(V_m^2 / 4*pi\) * int_0^pi \(1 - cos\(2*theta\)\) d\(theta\) = \(V_m^2 / 4*pi\) * [) Tj
T*
(theta - sin\(2*theta\)/2 ]_0^pi) Tj
T*
(= \(V_m^2 / 4*pi\) * \(pi - 0\) = V_m^2 / 4.) Tj
T*
(Taking square root: V_rms = V_m / 2 = 0.50 * V_m.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Compute Form Factor and Peak Factor:) Tj
T*
(Form Factor = V_rms / V_avg = \(V_m / 2\) / \(V_m / pi\) = pi / 2 ~ 1.57.) Tj
T*
(Peak Factor = V_m / V_rms = V_m / \(V_m / 2\) = 2.0.) Tj
