T*
(series AC circuit.) Tj
T*
(Answer: In a series RLC circuit, total impedance is Z = R + j*\(omega*L - 1/\(omega*C\)\).) Tj
T*
(Resonance occurs when the net reactive component vanishes: omega_0*L - 1/\(omega_0*C\) = 0) Tj
T*
(=> omega_0^2 = 1/\(LC\) => omega_0 = 1/sqrt\(LC\). Resonant frequency in Hertz: f_0 = 1 /) Tj
T*
([2*pi*sqrt\(LC\)]. At this frequency, Z = R, which is minimal, and current I_0 = V/R is) Tj
T*
(maximal. Quality Factor Q is defined as 2*pi * \(Maximum energy stored / Energy) Tj
T*
(dissipated per cycle\). This equals the ratio of reactive voltage across inductor to) Tj
T*
(applied supply voltage: Q = V_L / V = \(I_0 * omega_0 * L\) / \(I_0 * R\) = \(omega_0 * L\) /) Tj
T*
(R. Substituting omega_0 = 1/sqrt\(LC\) yields: Q = \(1 / R\) * sqrt\(L / C\).) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain the significance of Power Factor in industrial power distribution and) Tj
T*
(detail how shunt capacitors improve it.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Power factor PF = cos\(phi\) = P / S. Apparent power S = P / PF. For a fixed) Tj
T*
(active power P, a low lagging power factor forces the electrical supply to deliver) Tj
T*
(vastly higher current \(I = S / V\). High line current causes: \(1\) Excessive I^2*R copper) Tj
T*
